        </div>

        <div class="tour" role="tabpanel" id="tour-mock" aria-labelledby="tour-tab-mock" hidden>
          <div class="tour-copy">
            <h3>Build the frontend before the endpoint exists.</h3>
            <p>Save real responses as examples and serve the collection on localhost. Path templates like <code>/orders/:id</code> and recorded query values decide which example answers.</p>
            <ul class="ticks">
              <li>No request quota and no cloud account</li>
              <li>A live log of every call, including the ones nothing matched</li>
              <li>Edit an example and the running mock reloads</li>
              <li>Optionally replay the original response times</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="tour-link" href={href('docs/guides/mock-server/')}>How the mock matches requests →</a>
